{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller set is; in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not matter; isolated vertices are in it. Deterministic, but which minimum set it is depends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumDominatingSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (a leaf rule that settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest 2-packing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one smaller, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last set found is the answer. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(mean degree d with d² above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the component size in the worst case; the search does not check for task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1764"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","fragments":[{"ki